      "summary": "Zermatt: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 1: Zermatt: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Zermatt - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/zermatt-character.jpg)\n\nNestled at the head of the Mattertal valley at an elevation of sixteen hundred meters, Zermatt is the quintessential Swiss alpine wonderland. Looming directly above the village is the colossal, solitary pyramid of the Matterhorn, whose dramatic tooth of granite catches the earliest golden rays of dawn and the last fiery alpine glow of sunset. Traditional dark-timber Valais chalets, resting on stone mushroom pillars designed centuries ago to deter rodents, line the historic village center alongside luxury alpine lodges.\n\n![Geographic location of Zermatt in Switzerland](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/zermatt-map.png)\n\nElectric electro-taxis and horse-drawn carriages glide silently along narrow cobblestone streets, preserving the pristine alpine air. High above the valley floor, the Gornergrat cogwheel railway climbs steep pine slopes to open sweeping panoramas of twenty-nine peaks exceeding four thousand meters and sprawling glacial ice fields. In the quiet evenings, the soft lights of alpine chalets sparkle against the majestic mountain silhouette under an astonishing canopy of stars."
