      "title": "Cortina d'Ampezzo: Alpine Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Cortina d'Ampezzo: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 6: Cortina d'Ampezzo: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Cortina d'Ampezzo - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/cortina-dampezzo-character.jpg)\n\nKnown as the Queen of the Dolomites, Cortina d'Ampezzo is nestled in a wide, sunlit amphitheater surrounded by some of the most dramatic mountain spires on Earth. At dawn and twilight, the pale limestone towers of the Tofane, Cristallo, and Sorapiss mountains glow in ethereal shades of pink and orange—a breathtaking geological phenomenon known as enrosadira.\n\n![Geographic location of Cortina d'Ampezzo in Italy](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/cortina-dampezzo-map.png)\n\nThe vibrant pedestrian promenade of Corso Italia is flanked by upscale boutiques, art galleries, and historic alpine hotels, centered around the green-and-white stone bell tower of the Basilica of Saints Philip and James. Traditional Ladin culture survives in the surrounding hamlets, where rustic wooden barns and centuries-old mountain farmsteads sit peacefully against the jagged alpine horizon."
