      "summary": "Interlaken: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 7: Interlaken: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Interlaken - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/interlaken-character.jpg)\n\nSituated on a narrow alluvial plain between the shimmering turquoise waters of Lake Brienz and the deep blue expanse of Lake Thun, Interlaken is the legendary threshold to the Bernese Oberland. The town offers an unobstructed, postcard-perfect view up the Lütschine valley toward the majestic snow-capped triumvirate of the Eiger, Mönch, and Jungfrau mountains.\n\n![Geographic location of Interlaken in Switzerland](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/interlaken-map.png)\n\nAlong the grand promenade of the Höheweg, horse-drawn carriages pass manicured gardens, grand Belle Époque hotels, and the open expanse of the Höhematte park, where paragliders drift gracefully down from alpine cliffs. Historic steam paddle-wheelers cross the twin lakes, carrying travelers to roaring subterranean waterfalls and tranquil timber hamlets perched on verdant mountain slopes."
