      "summary": "Sintra: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 11: Sintra: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Sintra - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/sintra-character.jpg)\n\nRising dramatically from the Atlantic coastal plain, the lush, mist-shrouded granite hills of the Serra de Sintra have served as a sanctuary for Portuguese royalty and romantic poets for centuries. Densely forested slopes of giant ferns, moss-covered boulders, and exotic pine trees create an enchanted microclimate crowned by eccentric royal palaces.\n\n![Geographic location of Sintra in Portugal](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/sintra-map.png)\n\nAt the highest rocky pinnacle stands the Pena Palace, an astonishing Romanticist fantasy of vivid yellow and terracotta towers, neo-Manueline carvings, and ornate drawbridges. Deep in the forested valleys below, the mystical Quinta da Regaleira conceals labyrinthine gardens, subterranean grottos, and an astonishing inverted stone initiation well that spirals deep into the mountain bedrock."
