      "summary": "Ronda: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 12: Ronda: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Ronda - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/ronda-character.jpg)\n\nPerched high on a colossal limestone plateau in the Serranía de Ronda, this ancient Andalusian stronghold is cleft in two by the sheer, one-hundred-and-twenty-meter-deep El Tajo gorge. Connecting the historic Moorish medina with the eighteenth-century Mercadillo district is the monumental Puente Nuevo, a magnificent three-arched stone bridge whose central room once served as a prison.\n\n![Geographic location of Ronda in Spain](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/ronda-map.png)\n\nWhitewashed houses with wrought-iron balconies cling daringly to the edge of the vertical precipice, looking out across rolling olive groves and jagged mountain ridges. The town's historic bullring, one of the oldest and most revered in Spain, exemplifies neoclassical stone grandeur, while the terraced gardens of the Casa del Rey Moro descend via secret mine tunnels directly to the rushing river below."
