      "title": "Civita di Bagnoregio: Alpine Sanctuary",
      "summary": "Civita di Bagnoregio: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 13: Civita di Bagnoregio: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Civita di Bagnoregio - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/civita-di-bagnoregio-character.jpg)\n\nIsolated on a solitary pinnacle of volcanic tufa rock in the dramatic lunar valley of the Calanchi, Civita di Bagnoregio is known as 'the dying town' due to the constant erosion of its clay cliffs. Accessible only via a slender, three-hundred-meter pedestrian footbridge soaring above the ravines, entering the town feels like stepping back through centuries of silence.\n\n![Geographic location of Civita di Bagnoregio in Italy](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/civita-di-bagnoregio-map.png)\n\nFounded by the Etruscans over two thousand five hundred years ago, its medieval stone houses, ivy-covered Romanesque archways, and quiet central piazza have been meticulously preserved. Flower pots adorn ancient stone doorsteps, and cobblestone alleys end abruptly at sheer drops overlooking the sweeping, canyon-scored landscape of central Italy."
