      "content": "### Chapter 14: San Marino: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![San Marino - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/san-marino-character.jpg)\n\nClinging to the jagged limestone ridge of Mount Titano, the City of San Marino is the historic heart of the world's oldest surviving constitutional republic, founded in 301 AD. Three formidable medieval stone towers—Guaita, Cesta, and Montale—crown the three highest peaks of the mountain, linked by a picturesque paved battlements trail called the Path of Witches.\n\n![Geographic location of San Marino in San Marino](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/san-marino-map.png)\n\nNarrow, stepped cobblestone streets wind past ancient stone bastions, the neo-Gothic Palazzo Pubblico, and quiet panoramic terraces offering sweeping views of the green hills of Romagna stretching all the way to the blue Adriatic Sea. San Marino stands as a living symbol of unbroken independence and ancient mountain liberty."
