      "summary": "Albarracín: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 15: Albarracín: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Albarracín - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/albarracin-character.jpg)\n\nCradled in a dramatic loop of the Guadalaviar River in the rugged mountains of Aragon, Albarracín is often acclaimed as Spain's most beautiful village. Its unique architecture is characterized by warm pink and reddish-ochre plaster, curved timber beams of Sabina pine, and narrow, overhanging upper floors that almost touch across the steep cobblestone alleys.\n\n![Geographic location of Albarracín in Spain](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/albarracin-map.png)\n\nSurrounding the town, colossal fourteenth-century stone walls climb impossibly up the razor-sharp limestone ridge of the mountain, culminating in the imposing Tower of the Andador. From the ramparts, the view encompasses red-tiled roofs, the sixteenth-century cathedral spire, and the desolate, pine-covered wilderness of the Universal Mountains."
