      "summary": "Monsanto: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 16: Monsanto: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Monsanto - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/monsanto-character.jpg)\n\nPerched on a dramatic granite inselberg rising abruptly eight hundred meters above the rolling plains of the Beira Baixa, Monsanto is famous as Portugal's most Portuguese village. Over centuries, residents ingeniously constructed their stone cottages directly into, between, and beneath colossal moss-covered granite boulders, some weighing hundreds of tons.\n\n![Geographic location of Monsanto in Portugal](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/monsanto-map.png)\n\nTiny cottages feature granite boulders serving as living room walls, roofs, and doorposts. At the summit of the peak stand the haunting stone ruins of a Templar fortress, offering breathtaking three-hundred-and-sixty-degree vistas across olive groves to the Spanish border. Wandering its steep, boulder-strewn alleys is an unforgettable journey through human adaptability and ancient stone craftsmanship."
