      "summary": "Matera: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 17: Matera: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Matera - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/matera-character.jpg)\n\nMatera is one of the oldest continuously inhabited cities on earth, its history etched into the soft calcareous rock of the Sassi districts. Thousands of pale tufa houses, cave dwellings, and subterranean cisterns are stacked upon each other along the cliffs of a dramatic river canyon, creating a labyrinth of stone terraces where the roof of one house serves as the street for the one above.\n\n![Geographic location of Matera in Italy](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/matera-map.png)\n\nOver one hundred and fifty rupestrian churches carved directly into the rock feature Byzantine-style frescoes preserved for a thousand years. As dusk falls, warm golden lanterns illuminate the pale stone amphitheater of the Sasso Caveoso and Sasso Barisano, transforming the ancient gorge into an evocative, timeless nativity scene beneath starry Mediterranean skies."
