      "summary": "Meteora: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 18: Meteora: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Meteora - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/meteora-character.jpg)\n\nRising dramatically from the plain of Thessaly near the town of Kalabaka, Meteora—meaning 'suspended in the air'—is one of the most astonishing geological and spiritual wonders in the world. Towering monolithic sandstone pillars, sculpted by millions of years of wind and water, soar up to four hundred meters into the Greek sky.\n\n![Geographic location of Meteora in Greece](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/meteora-map.png)\n\nPerched atop these sheer, inaccessible rock towers are six active fourteenth-century Eastern Orthodox monasteries, originally reached only by long ladders lashed together or windlasses hauling rope nets. Inside, stone courtyards, wooden balconies overhanging dizzying abysses, and fresco-adorned chapels preserve centuries of ascetic devotion and Byzantine art amid breathtaking panoramas of the Pindus mountain range."
