      "summary": "Mostar: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 19: Mostar: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Mostar - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/mostar-character.jpg)\n\nNestled in a deep valley between the mountains of Hum and Velež, Mostar is a cultural crossroads where Ottoman Islamic heritage and Balkan stone craftsmanship intertwine. The soul of the city is the Stari Most (Old Bridge), a graceful single-arch stone masterpiece constructed in 1566 by the Ottoman architect Mimar Hajrudin, soaring twenty-four meters above the icy turquoise waters of the Neretva River.\n\n![Geographic location of Mostar in Bosnia & Herzegovina](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/mostar-map.png)\n\nThe surrounding historic Kujundžiluk bazaar is paved with smooth river cobbles and lined with copper artisan workshops, traditional carpet shops, and outdoor cafes serving rich Bosnian coffee in engraved dzezvas. Slender stone minarets like that of the Koski Mehmed Pasha Mosque punctuate the skyline, offering dizzying panoramas of red-clay and slate roofs nestled between dramatic mountain slopes."
