      "summary": "Berat: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 20: Berat: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Berat - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/berat-character.jpg)\n\nStraddling the Osum River beneath the dramatic limestone ridge of Mount Tomorr, Berat is acclaimed as Albania's City of a Thousand Windows. The historic Mangalem and Gorica quarters feature tiers of Ottoman whitewashed stone houses with endless rows of dark-framed rectangular windows climbing steeply up the hillside, creating an architectural facade of mesmerizing symmetry.\n\n![Geographic location of Berat in Albania](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/berat-map.png)\n\nHigh above the river rises the colossal thirteenth-century Kalaja fortress, which remains a living citadel with stone houses, Byzantine churches, and Ottoman ruins within its massive walls. An ancient multi-arched stone bridge links the Christian and Muslim quarters across the emerald river, celebrating a centuries-old tradition of religious harmony and mountain hospitality."
