      "summary": "Ohrid: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 21: Ohrid: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Ohrid - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/ohrid-character.jpg)\n\nPerched on the eastern shore of Lake Ohrid—one of Europe's oldest and deepest aquatic ecosystems—the historic city of Ohrid was once known as the Slavic Jerusalem for its three hundred and sixty-five churches. Narrow cobblestone streets climb the steep mountain crest crowned by the monumental stone ramparts of Samuel's Fortress.\n\n![Geographic location of Ohrid in North Macedonia](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/ohrid-map.png)\n\nThe city's most iconic sight is the thirteenth-century Church of Saint John at Kaneo, perched on a dramatic cliff edge jutting out over the crystal-clear waters of the lake. Down in the Old Bazaar, artisan workshops craft traditional Ohrid pearls from the scales of endemic Plasica fish, while waterfront promenades line tranquil pebble beaches surrounded by the rugged Galichica mountain peaks."
