      "summary": "Zakopane: Alpine Sanctuary - Cities of Wonder: 40 Most Beautiful Cities in the World, Volume 3",
      "content": "### Chapter 22: Zakopane: Alpine Sanctuary\n\n![Zakopane - Iconic mountain view](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/zakopane-character.jpg)\n\nNestled in the southern valley beneath the jagged granite crags of the High Tatras, Zakopane is the winter capital of Poland and the heart of the proud Highlander (Goral) culture. The town is famous for the Zakopane Style of architecture, pioneered by Stanisław Witkiewicz, featuring ornate wooden villas built of massive larch logs with steeply pitched shingled roofs, intricately carved decorative sunbursts, and floral motifs.\n\n![Geographic location of Zakopane in Poland](https://assets.lingocafe.app/cities-03/images/zakopane-map.png)\n\nAlong the bustling pedestrian street of Krupówki, street vendors roast traditional smoked Oscypek sheep's milk cheese on open grills while folk fiddlers play energetic mountain tunes. Cable cars ascend to Mount Gubałówka, offering sweeping vistas of the legendary sleeping knight profile of Mount Giewont and the alpine summits of Tatra National Park."
